# Sync Task Schema to Base44 Cloud

## Goal Description

Sync the local `Task` entity schema to Base44 Cloud to resolve valid schema expectations and enable backend operations like [CuriosityEngine](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/swarm/core/curiosity_engine.ts#14-99). The current app configuration points to a frontend-only app, preventing schema pushes. We will create/link a new Backend App.

## Proposed Changes

### Configuration
#### [MODIFY] [base44/entities/task.jsonc](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/base44/entities/task.jsonc)
- Change `name` to `Task` to match SDK usage.

#### [MODIFY] [base44/config.jsonc](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/base44/config.jsonc)

- Update `appId` to point to the new Backend App.

#### [MODIFY] [.env.local](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/.env.local)

- Update `BASE44_APP_ID` and `VITE_BASE44_APP_ID` to the new App ID.

### Schema Pushing

- Run `npx base44 entities push` to sync [base44/entities/task.jsonc](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/base44/entities/task.jsonc).

## Verification Plan

### Automated Verification

- Detailed logs from `npx base44 entities push`.
- Check `npx base44 entities list` to verify `task` entity exists on cloud.

### Manual Verification

- Trigger [CuriosityEngine](file:///c:/Users/ferna/Downloads/appforge-main/swarm/core/curiosity_engine.ts#14-99) to verify it can interact with the new app without 422 errors (or with different errors related to schema validation that we can then fix).
